<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Việt Nam Quốc Dân Đảng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1927</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Vietnamese Nationalist Party, VNQDĐ, Viet Nam Quoc Dan Dang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Việt Nam Quốc Dân Đảng, or Vietnamese Nationalist Party, was a revolutionary party founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a> in 1927 by Nguyễn Thái Học and others, modelled on the Chinese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a>. It aimed to overthrow French rule by armed revolt, but the failed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yen-bai-mutiny">Yên Bái mutiny</a> of February 1930 led to the execution of its leaders. It survived in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and later opposed the communists.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/viet-nam-quoc-dan-dang.jpg" alt="Việt Nam Quốc Dân Đảng" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aogiapvang · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_VNQDD.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
